      "message": "in linux:\n\n#define KEY_CHANNELUP\t\t0x192\t/* Channel Increment */\n#define KEY_CHANNELDOWN\t\t0x193\t/* Channel Decrement */\n#define KEY_FIRST\t\t0x194\n#define KEY_LAST\t\t0x195\t/* Recall Last */\n\n\nSo the keycode KEY_LAST is related to TV, because it\u0027s in the vicinity of other TV-related keys. Therefore, I think mapping this to LAST_CHANNEL is OK.\n\nIt would be nice if we could specify \"KEY_LAST\" instead of having to use a decimal number, and then having to convert to hex before being able to find it on https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/include/uapi/linux/input-event-codes.h",
